[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Restart Emacs after installation.

To use Mozc as your default input method, add the following line
to your Emacs initialization file, such as ~/.emacs or
~/.emacs.d/init.el:

(setq default-input-method "japanese-mozc")

Press C-\ to toggle Japanese input.

To select Mozc without changing your initialization file, use:

M-x set-input-method RET japanese-mozc RET

The helper program's path is configured by this port.
The Mozc server starts automatically when needed.
No IBus or Fcitx configuration is required for use within Emacs.

If you prefer C-o for toggling input, you can optionally add:

(global-set-key (kbd "C-o") 'toggle-input-method)

This replaces the standard C-o binding for open-line.
EOM
}
]
